   "text": "That ratio is the entire reason a cache exists: it turns 116,000 reads/sec into about 5,800/sec reaching the\ndatabase. And the redirect must resolve in under 50ms at p99 - it is invisible latency inside someone else's\npage load, so when it is slow, the DESTINATION site is what feels slow.",
